# PDF files carry meaningful byte offsets internally (the xref table);
# converting LF<->CRLF on checkout, which Windows git's core.autocrlf
# does by default for anything it heuristically guesses is text, shifts
# every one of those offsets and corrupts the file ("Unexpected EOF" on
# open). PDFs are text-heavy enough in their header/xref/trailer sections
# to fool that heuristic, so they need an explicit binary declaration;
# .npz/.xlsx are zip-based and are reliably auto-detected as binary
# already, but are marked explicitly here too rather than relying on it.
*.pdf binary
*.npz binary
*.xlsx binary
